From 8d10641ca112ac371c9bd82e18dd60bdc98c1ef1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: patricksmithlaravel <patricksmithlaravel@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 6 Oct 2026 18:46:04 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] android: exit on Destroy, allow a new loop, report inset
 changes

Android can destroy an activity and start a new one in the same process,
for a configuration change the manifest does not take (font scale,
locale, night mode, navigation mode). Both glues wait in onDestroy, on
the Java main thread, for android_main to return, but the loop ignored
MainEvent::Destroy, so the activity hung and the app hit an ANR. The
loop now exits on Destroy. Input is not read after Destroy: there is
none, and GameActivity (android-activity 0.6.1) would only log an error.

The next activity's android_main, like a launch after the app ended its
loop, then failed to build an EventLoop with RecreationAttempt. Dropping
the EventLoop now resets the one-loop-per-process guard.

ContentRectChanged (NativeActivity and GameActivity) and InsetsChanged
(GameActivity) are reported as WindowEvent::Resized once the native
window exists, so the app knows to read the new content rect or insets.
The size may be unchanged; the iOS backend also reports a Resized on
every layout of its view, safe-area changes included.

This is winit PR #4739 with three additions: ContentRectChanged is
reported too (NativeActivity has no InsetsChanged, so the PR's inset
change never reached it), input is skipped after Destroy, and the
EventLoopBuilder::build docs and the changelog describe the change.

Verified: cargo check for aarch64-linux-android and x86_64-linux-android
with android-native-activity and with android-game-activity, for
aarch64-apple-ios, wasm32 and the host; cargo clippy -D warnings on both
Android targets and features; cargo doc for Android; cargo +nightly fmt
--check; cargo test on the host. On an API 36 arm64 emulator, with a
NativeActivity probe app:
- Changing the font scale twice relaunched the activity in the same
  process each time: Suspended, LoopExiting, run_app returned, and the
  next android_main built its loop. No ANR. With v0.30.13 the loop
  stopped after Suspended and the app hit an input ANR.
- Ending the loop from the app and launching again built a new loop in
  the same process. With v0.30.13 the build failed with
  RecreationAttempt.
- With targetSdk 34, showing and hiding the keyboard each gave a Resized
  with the new content rect (bottom 2337, 1517, 2337). The PR as posted
  gave none.
GameActivity was checked by compiling only.
